Description: base_unittests' SystemAllocatorTest tests glibc's allocator entry points, which musl doesn't have: it would fail to link.
Forwarded: not-needed (copium's; its author sends what fits upstream)
Origin: copium 155.2 (https://codeberg.org/selfisekai/copium: the musl patches Alpine's chromium applies), cr149-musl-alloc-shim-dispatch.patch
The author's e-mail address is left out of the From line below.

From d8b94093a10ef34c2a7e80d1d6fec7e75b476547 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LN Liberda
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 04:23:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] musl: Disable SystemAllocatorTest

Tests otherwise unused code, which we'd notice to be used because it fails to link.
---
 base/BUILD.gn | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/base/BUILD.gn b/base/BUILD.gn
index 16fd234a12b25..4059dcb502425 100644
--- a/base/BUILD.gn
+++ b/base/BUILD.gn
@@ -4029,7 +4029,7 @@ test("base_unittests") {
     "//testing/buildbot/filters:base_unittests_filters",
   ]
 
-  if (is_win || is_linux) {
+  if (is_win || is_linux && false) {
     data_deps += [ "//base/allocator:system_allocator_test_helper" ]
     sources += [ "allocator/system_allocator_unittest.cc" ]
   }
